[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Architecture Overview

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: High Level System Architecture

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
.. raw:: html

   <pre class="mermaid">
   flowchart TB

    FW["Main Control<br/>Firmware"]
    EEPROM["EEPROM"]

    subgraph HI["Head Interface"]

        GPIO["GPIO"]
        PROC["Processing"]
        ADC["ADC"]
        SPI["SPI"]
        UART["UART"]
        I2C["I2C"]

        GPIO --- PROC
        PROC --- ADC

        SPI --- PROC
        UART --- PROC
        I2C --- PROC
    end

    SPI <--> EEPROM
    UART <--> FW

    Lasers <-- GPIO
    Interlocks --> GPIO
    Buttons --> GPIO

    Magnetometers --> I2C
    I2C --> LEDRing["LED Ring"]

    ADC <--> Temp["Temperature<br/>Sensor"]
    ADC <--> Pressure["Pressure<br/>Sensor"]
    ADC <--> Flow["Flow<br/>Sensor"]
   </pre>
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Main Modules

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
Processing Loop - The main loop processes analog and digital signals and uses them to report Head
subsystem data back to the Main Control Firmware. Requests from the main control firmware are also
handled and responded to such as changing the output state of the LED Ring.

Buttons - The Head Interface reads 5 GPIO buttons that can change the function for the user.

Lasers - GPIO output controls low power positioning lasers.

LED Ring - RGB LED's controlled by a UART signal that determines color, brightness, and behavior.

Analog Sensors - The Head Interface reads analog signal data from Water Temperature, Pressure, and
Flow sensors. This analog data is processed and then reported to the Main Control firmware. Sensors
can determine limits that may trigger a fault condition.

Digital Sensors - The Head Interface reads digital data from Magnetometer IC's mounted near the
deflecting coils. This data is processed and then reported to the Main Control firmware. These sensors
can create responses such as coil level adjustments or possibly fault conditions.

EEPROM - Nonvolatile data storage.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
PREFIX: SW-H1FHI-
TITLE: Design Items

[DESIGN_ITEM]
UID: SW-H1FHI-26
TITLE: Manufacturer Hardware Abstraction
STATEMENT: >>>
The firmware integrates source code provided by the manufacturer of the microcontroller unit to
interface with various peripherals of the microcontroller. These include functions to interface with
the following peripherals of the microcontroller:

- UART serial port

- I2C serial port

- ADC peripheral

- Pulse width modulation (PWM)

- GPIO
<<<
